          $VER: FPBadUploadMailer, v1.00 (30-Jun-96) by Dotoran!
-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

Disclaimer:
~~~~~~~~~~
    Originally, v.02 was written by PMK, aka Peter Klein. Since Peter has
decided to go the IBM route, I'll be attempting to "take on" the continued
development of the files he has authored in the past.

What Is It?
~~~~~~~~~~
    This mod allows you to send the UPLOADER of a file you are considering
[K]illing a piece of mail. Perhaps you DID kill/delete the file, and wish
to send a message telling the uploader WHY the file was killed, or perhaps
there's something WRONG with the file, and it MAY be killed shortly, unless
the uploader does something(describes it, finishes uploading it, etc.)

    When you use the "K" command to kill a file, you'll first be asked if
you wish the "post" killed, then you'll be asked if you wish to "Notify the
Uploader". If you say YES, you'll see this programs menu, where you'll be
able to choose from 5 pre-written messages, or create one of your own.

How Do I Install It?
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
1. Copy the "FPBUM/" directory into your "FPFiles/" directory if you have
   one, or else copy the "FPFiles/FPBUM/" directory anywhere on your system.

   NOTE: All Dotoran released "FP" files will be stored in the "FPFiles/"
         directory, in order to make working with them a bit easier, so it
         is HIGHLY recommended that you do the same on your systems...

2. Load your BBSTEXT file into an editor, then add the following to the
   beginning of line 1830: (The following should be placed ON ONE LINE,
   and is broken into two lines below for readability purposes only!}:

        Notify uploader? [No]: \?0{T70 #1}{JN 1+}
        {#0<path>FPFiles/FPBUM/FPBUM}{1}

   NOTE: Replace <path> with the one you used in Step # 1 above. Change the
         one \ and four {'s into a Control-Y and Control-Q characters, and
         remember, the above should be placed ON ONE LINE before the text
         found on line 1830. ("Delete this File [Yes]?")

3. There are 5 text files included inside the "FPFiles/FPBUM/" directory
   that you may wish to edit further in one of CNet's editors. You can use
   CNet's WF command to edit these files. To make customizing these files
   a bit more powerful, you can include special ¹ keywords. The ¹ can be
   created by pressing ALT-1 on your keyboard. The following is a list of
   the available keywords that can be used: (case does NOT matter)

             KEYWORD:   DESCRIPTION OF VALUE:
             ~~~~~~~    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
              ¹FILE     Name of File.
              ¹AREA     Filearea. (Subboard Name)
              ¹RFAC     Credit removal factor.
              ¹BCRE     Size of the file in Bytes.
              ¹FCRE     Size of file in File Credits.
              ¹HAND     Uploader's Handle.
              ¹NAME     Uploader's Real Name.
              ¹BTOT     Uploader's Total Byte Credits.
              ¹FTOT     Uploader's Total File Credits.
              ¹BRAT     Uploader's BYTE RATIO Default (#1)
              ¹FRAT     Uploader's FILE RATIO Default (#1)
              ¹DATE     Date file was Uploaded.
              ¹BBSN     Your BBS's Name (from Config).

   Keywords will be translated before the mail is sent. If you opt to edit
   one of the pre-defined letters before it is sent, you'll see the actual
   data in place of the keywords. If you opt to "Create New Mail", without
   using one of the predefined letters, you should NOT use keywords in the
   text, as they will NOT be translated before being sent to the user's
   mailbox.

4. That's It! You can reload your BBSTEXT, and you'll be ready to use the
   FPBUM mod! Enjoy!
                                                                - Dotoran
